2. **Optional version bump** — Resolve publish-on-success first when applicable (see **Publish-on-success label** above): if `issue-flow agent publish-intent --issue <N> --json` reports `matched: true` and not ops, treat it as a bump request at `level` / `target_version` (stop-and-ask when `logical` is false or `conflict` is true). Then, if the user asked for a bump (see above), follow `{{ agent_dir }}/skills/iflow-version-bump/SKILL.md` — it resolves the project's **release strategy** first (the "Release & version bump" section of `{{ issueflows_dir }}/{{ designs_folder }}/this-project.md`, else `pyproject.toml` detection, else the uv default). **Static version:** run `uv version --bump <level>` (or set the explicit target when the label named a version). **Git-tag derived:** edit nothing — compute and report the **planned tag** (e.g. `v1.0.4a3`), record it in the status file, and defer creating it until after the merge (step 9 with `yolo`, else `/iflow-cleanup`). If neither strategy applies, skip and continue.{% if confirm_version_bump %} Without the `yolo` token, if the user did **not** request a bump **and** there is no publish label, ask once whether to bump before continuing (skip asking under `yolo`).{% endif %}

{% if defer_changelog %}3. **Decide the changelog bullet (do not write `{{ history_file }}`)** — Unless the user passed `nohistory`, follow `{{ agent_dir }}/skills/iflow-history-update/SKILL.md` to *compose* the bullet (issue title, or `log "..."` / `note "..."` text). **Do not edit** `{{ history_file }}` on the issue branch — this project has `defer_changelog = true`.{% if confirm_changelog_update %} Show the proposed bullet and confirm once before recording. If declined, **stop** — offer record / revise / `nohistory` / abort; do not continue close without an explicit choice.{% else %} Record without a confirm prompt (`confirm_changelog_update` is false).{% endif %} With the `yolo` token, do not ask — decide yourself. Write a `### Deferred changelog` section on `issue<N>_status.md` with the bullet (and `Planned version: <ver>` when step 2 bumped or planned a version; or `nohistory` when skipped). Put the same bullet in the PR body. `issue-flow agent apply-changelog --issue N` writes `{{ history_file }}` on the default branch after merge (`/iflow-cleanup` A1 / yolo post-pull).
